Input: {"question": "What political party is Senator Atkinson a part of?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00", "text": "Archibald Atkinson Archibald Atkinson (September 15, 1792 – January 7, 1872) was a U.S. Representative from Virginia. Born in Isle of Wight County, Virginia, Atkinson received a liberal education. He attended the law department of the College of William & Mary (now the Marshall-Wythe School of Law), Williamsburg, Virginia. He served during the War of 1812. He was admitted to the bar and commenced practice in Smithfield, Virginia. He was a member of the Virginia House of Delegates 1815–1817 and 1828–1831, and served in the Virginia Senate 1839–1843. Atkinson was elected as a Democrat to the Twenty-eighth, Twenty-ninth, and Thirtieth"}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01", "text": "Jason Atkinson Jason Atkinson (born November 6, 1970) is an American politician in the US state of Oregon. The Republican grew up in the Southern Oregon city of Ashland. He served as a senator in the Oregon State Senate from 2001 to 2013. He ran unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon in 2006, but was reelected to the Senate in 2008. He stated his intention to run in the 2010 Oregon gubernatorial election, but withdrew from the race in 2009. In 1998, Atkinson was elected to his first public office as a member of the Oregon House"}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d02", "text": "Check out iVoterGuide JavaScript is disabled in your browser . Please enable JavaScript to use this application ."}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03", "text": "our professional staff of editors , writers , and researchers . Click here to contact our editorial staff or report an error . For media inquiries , contact us here . Please donate here to support our continued expansion . Information about voting Your 2025 Election Toolkit What 's on my ballot ? Where do I vote ? How do I register to vote ? How do I request a ballot ? W